<article class="env-lemma" id="0E01">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0E01">Lemma <span data-tag="0E01">66.22.6</span>.</a> Let $S$ be a scheme. Let $X$ be an algebraic space over $S$. Let $x \in |X|$ be a point. The following are equivalent </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
the local ring of $X$ at $x$ is reduced (Remark <a href="/tag/0BBL" data-tag="0BBL">66.7.6</a>), 
</p>
</li><li><p>
$\mathcal{O}_{X, \overline{x}}$ is reduced for some geometric point $\overline{x}$ lying over $x$, and 
</p>
</li><li><p>
$\mathcal{O}_{X, \overline{x}}$ is reduced for any geometric point $\overline{x}$ lying over $x$. 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      The equivalence of (2) and (3) follows from the fact that the isomorphism type of $\mathcal{O}_{X, \overline{x}}$ only depends on $x \in |X|$, see Remark <a href="/tag/04K4" data-tag="04K4">66.19.11</a>. Using Lemma <a href="/tag/04KF" data-tag="04KF">66.22.1</a> the equivalence of (1) and (2)$+$(3) comes down to the following statement: a local ring is reduced if and only if its strict henselization is reduced. This is More on Algebra, Lemma <a href="/tag/06DH" data-tag="06DH">15.46.4</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>